{"path":"std/fs/fn.remove_dir.html","title":"Function remove_dir","description":"Removes an empty directory.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function remove_dir"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/fs.rs.html#3121-3123","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"pub fn remove_dir<P: AsRef<Path>>(path: P) -> Result<()>"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Removes an empty directory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to remove a directory that is not empty, as well as all of its contents recursively, consider using "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/fn.remove_dir_all.html","title":"fn std::fs::remove_dir_all","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"remove_dir_all"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instead."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"platform-specific-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform-specific behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function currently corresponds to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"rmdir"},{"type":"text","value":" function on Unix and the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"RemoveDirectory"},{"type":"text","value":" function on Windows. Note that, this "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/index.html#platform-specific-behavior","title":"mod std::io","children":[{"type":"text","value":"may change in the future"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will return an error in the following situations, but is not limited to just these cases:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" doesn’t exist."}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"path"},{"type":"text","value":" isn’t a directory."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The user lacks permissions to remove the directory at the provided "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"path"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The directory isn’t empty."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will only ever return an error of kind "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NotFound"},{"type":"text","value":" if the given path does not exist. Note that the inverse is not true, i.e. if a path does not exist, its removal may fail for a number of reasons, such as insufficient permissions."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::fs;\n\nfn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {\n    fs::remove_dir(\"/some/dir\")?;\n    Ok(())\n}"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Ause+std::fs;%0A%0Afn+main()+-%3E+std::io::Result%3C()%3E+%7B%0A++++fs::remove_dir(%22/some/dir%22)?;%0A++++Ok(())%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]}]}}
